Sam Dennis <sam@malfunction.screaming.net> writes:
> steve lefevre wrote:
> > What's the best way to get the goodies from a dart/arrow trap? Does letting
> > them hit you give as many as it would if you disabled them?
> 
> It has the potential to give many more, without limit (in old versions,
> it would always do so if you possessed sufficient patience), but better
> results should be seen when disarming, unless your luck is really dire.
> (Maybe not even then; it looks close, but I'm not going to work out the
> precise means right now.)

The optimum strategy may well be to try to get a certain number to
fire, then disarm; and it will depend whether you want to maximise
expected return, or whether you place a higher importance on getting
_something_ (utility per missile decreases with increased number,
after all).

> > There sometimes seems to be differences as to whether the resulting
> > projectiles are cursed or poisoned, as if the trap mechanism
> > curses/poisons them when it is sprung.  Is that true?
> 
> AFAICS, there is no difference in the probabilities, but the projectiles
> gained by disarming a trap will be all the same.

Arrows from a trap will never be poisoned; a fired dart has a 1/6 chance
of being poisoned, while the darts from disarming only have the standard
1/100 chance. buc and enchantment will be the standard weapon distribution
in either case.

